The game generates a lot more daggers than knives.  Soldiers
have equal chances of getting a knife or dagger among their
other options.  Hobbits, dwarves, orcs, elves and so on can
have daggers but never knives in their initial inventories.

While knives are individually better for throwing if both knives
and daggers are at unskilled, the game never seems to create
enough to have a quiver filled with them.  Except worm teeth
which don't do enough damage.  I don't recall amassing a
stack of a dozen knives by any method other than polypiling.
Not even Ludios has generated a dozen knives for me.  Next
time I get both castles I need to make a point of counting how
many knives I could gather from the mines plus the two
castles ...

Eventually inventory letters get valuable and it's likely a
player will need to choose between a partial stack of under a
dozen knives made up for with a partial stack of elven daggers
for 2 inventory letters, or a full stack of a dozen daggers.
That's in addition to daggers maybe getting unrestricted from
a divine gift.  There always seem to be enough elves and
hobbits generated to ensure that I have a dozen elven daggers
by the time I hit Medusa.

It looks to me like very early strategy would be to use everything
but the iron ball as a missile.  Then gradually build up a quiver
of knives and/or daggers until you have a "dozen" of them.
Then chose between a stack each of knives and daggers or a
single stack of the heavier daggers.  The weight of knives do
suggest using them as they are available in the early game,
though.



